Notebook[{
Cell["A Probe for the Document View Controls", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"dc57bbad-883a-463b-9462-19d002485cc9"],

Cell["MathNotebook", "Author",ExpressionUUID->"09cde4b4-1cf4-49d1-abf3-5acdb3597829"],

Cell["T6 \[AHat]\.80\.94 feedback round", "Date",ExpressionUUID->"e16a17d6-9845-46ff-90f7-4a6d15c0f5f6"],

Cell["\<\
Every style the two sliders are supposed to reach appears below exactly once, \
in the order the stylesheet declares them. Drag a slider and read down the \
page: a style that does not move is a defect. The text slider should move \
everything except the two displays and the equation number; the math slider \
should move only those three.\
\>", "Abstract",ExpressionUUID->"a556c6d2-2396-4a97-82bb-b4bd9f5d429c"],

Cell["What to Check", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"1378976c-4759-4b07-aef7-1ece19aeeb90"],

Cell["\<\
These are the things no script can verify, because a headless front end has \
no window and nothing ever gets clicked. They are the whole reason this round \
runs by hand.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3e5cfe07-e2c7-4318-b56f-ba525cad7eb5"],

Cell["\<\
Clicking a group header folds it, and the palette window refits to the new \
height immediately rather than on the next open.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"ed21a0c9-ea03-4761-8e16-e7456202c3af"],

Cell["\<\
Fold state comes back after quitting and reopening the front end.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"0af39139-7d8e-494d-9a30-62b86e34f011"],

Cell["\<\
Both sliders follow the focused document: click into another notebook and the \
readouts change to that document's sizes.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"70b96ba3-cdc4-407b-a72a-691a48f6c7c5"],

Cell["\<\
Releasing a slider actually applies the size \[Dash] dragging alone should \
not, and the release should.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"7d803fb3-bb13-48c7-9fd0-19462eac1fa4"],

Cell["\<\
Reset view returns this document to the sizes it has right now, with no trace \
left behind.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"f1404f58-0f15-46ee-b3f0-080b2f026039"],

Cell["\<\
The palette is comfortable to keep open beside a paper you are actually \
writing.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"58df2454-80e7-4795-93df-6257603b05e6"],

Cell["Prose and Sectioning", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"952e8ad0-6113-499e-885d-c75cb08172e1"],

Cell["\<\
Body text, the anchor of the text slider. This paragraph is deliberately long \
enough to wrap several times at every size in the slider's range, because the \
number of wrapped lines is the only honest read on whether a font size \
actually changed \[AHat]\.80\.94 the glyphs alone are easy to misjudge by eye.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a3187c59-0ad4-4cbb-90be-faa6f19547d8"],

Cell["A Subsection", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"9b8a0181-56d4-4577-9b6b-97fe226f6486"],

Cell["\<\
A second paragraph under a subsection, with inline mathematics \[Sum] \
\[Alpha] \[CenterDot] \[Beta] \[Element] \[DoubleStruckCapitalR] set in the \
body font, so prose and mathematics can be compared in one line.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1cba22b7-bd45-4582-b1fa-303a46b627c2"],

Cell["A Subsubsection", "Subsubsection",ExpressionUUID->"38f886f4-0f5a-45a2-a231-31e18186dd91"],

Cell["Prose under a subsubsection.", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"11d3ddad-c74a-46db-870d-9d2aef4e482d"],

Cell["Mathematics", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"171c7610-bb52-4713-9e4d-a49b7bac234b"],

Cell["\<\
An unnumbered display follows, then a numbered one. The equation number is \
its own style and has to grow with the mathematics, not with the prose.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ee2869a2-b357-4e1b-ad86-7aefa2c816ee"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  SubscriptBox["\[Integral]", "\[CapitalOmega]"], "d", "\[Omega]", "=", 
  SubscriptBox["\[Integral]", 
   RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "\[CapitalOmega]"}]], 
  "\[Omega]"}]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"1cd1e494-2b8d-4461-b70a-\
9aa758c4ab9d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalDelta]", "k"], "=", "d", 
  SuperscriptBox["d", "*"], "+", 
  SuperscriptBox["d", "*"], "d"}]], "DisplayFormulaNumbered",ExpressionUUID->\
"3cdad40a-138d-485a-b8aa-792fefeba1e2"],

Cell["Environments", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"1b35783f-d484-4de8-b559-2483c44f5e2a"],

Cell["\<\
A plain-class environment. It is declared to inherit from Text, so it carries \
no bare font size of its own and was one of the styles the text slider used \
to miss entirely.\
\>", "Theorem",ExpressionUUID->"485c75c0-0192-42b7-99c5-7d886d0675c1"],

Cell["\<\
The proof style, which inherits from Text in the same way. Both should now \
track the text slider; if either stays put, that is the session 6 fix \
regressing.\
\>", "Proof",ExpressionUUID->"7634b140-0b53-4fa6-845c-4521bc622e7d"],

Cell["A definition-class environment, upright rather than italic.", \
"Definition",ExpressionUUID->"22cc67e4-7d20-407b-bed4-3c886f22df0d"],

Cell["A remark-class environment, with an italic dingbat.", "Remark",ExpressionUUID->"6e1cb3f4-0752-4c43-927a-8720951db7a4"],

Cell["Lists", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"8db39fac-d397-4afc-8041-03a05ee4369b"],

Cell["\<\
The three list styles come from Default.nb, not from LaTeXBase.nb.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5a0c8236-8213-4228-8174-7d6ba2cc7802"],

Cell["An item.", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"9b69754c-1493-424e-b7e5-5c646ead99cb"],

Cell["A numbered item.", "ItemNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"efe76e31-3bc2-40ed-a23d-bb9948b3503e"],

Cell["An item paragraph.", "ItemParagraph",ExpressionUUID->"48b86f71-3ca0-495f-843b-4d4915bcdd2e"],

Cell["References", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"b095d46c-9c82-40d5-aa87-21949f84ec3d"],

Cell["\<\
Ollivier, Ricci curvature of Markov chains on metric spaces, \
https://arxiv.org/abs/0810.5625\
\>", "Reference",ExpressionUUID->"695d9025-9b7b-406f-9e7f-2a350fd593f1"],

Cell["\<\
Forman, Bochner's method for cell complexes and combinatorial Ricci \
curvature, Discrete Comput. Geom. 29 (2003) 323\[Dash]374\
\>", "Reference",ExpressionUUID->"80758b58-4d45-420b-a001-ae6358264daf"]
},
WindowSize->{900, 800},
